{"version":"1","id":"readrust","handle":"readrust","name":"Read Rust","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/be58d4b7ebe8474d8cb05d50625b2fe5","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-3.5435,"y":-2.8047,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":300,"newest_post_at":"2023-03-09T00:22:32.455Z","oldest_post_at":"2019-10-15T12:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.003333,"listicle_ratio":0.003333,"question_ratio":0.026667,"avg_read_time":23.257732,"summary_length_avg":313.83209,"title_length_avg":41.02,"title_length_var":319.3796,"tag_entropy":2.892382,"tag_diversity":0.306667,"top_tag_share":0.283333,"avg_upvotes":0.566667,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.01,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.023392,"zero_engagement_share":0.836667,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":2.174167,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.003333,"recency_skew":0.06383},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-5.4265,-5.6176],"cadence_depth":[4.9118,9.0],"hype_variety":[-2.4706,-3.2059],"title_style":[2.5735,0.5735]},"top_tags":[["rust",216],["general-programming",64],["c",28],["linux",16],["embedded",11],["github",9],["webdev",8],["testing",7]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Why is building a UI in Rust so hard?","zerocal - A Serverless Calendar App in Rust Running on shuttle.rs","Announcing the Rust Style Team"],"outlier":["Tauri vs Iced vs egui: Rust GUI framework performance comparison (including startup time, input lag, resize tests) \u00b7 Lukas\u02bc Blog"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"k7uD0KM3f","title":"Without boats, dreams dry up","url":"https://without.boats/blog/the-registers-of-rust/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/without-boats-dreams-dry-up-k7ud0km3f","summary":"The Registers of Rust - Without boats, dreams dry up. It\u2019s been nearly two and half years since I was an active contributor to the Rust project. I\u2019ve felt a certain apprehension at a lot of the directions the project has taken, which has often occupied my thoughts.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--qPvKM23u--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2009","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-09T00:22:32.455Z"},{"id":"53ue7iACs","title":"Reducing code size in librsvg by removing an unnecessary generic struct","url":"https://viruta.org/reducing-binary-size-generics.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/reducing-code-size-in-librsvg-by-removing-an-unnecessary-generic-struct-53ue7iacs","summary":"The post discusses the process of reducing code size in librsvg by removing an unnecessary generic struct. It explains how cargo-bloat can be used to estimate code size, the changes made to the code, and the impact it had on memory usage. The post also mentions the use of generics in code and provides alternative approaches to handle them.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/bfb8a26b40d6b7a1c758c0c6ee0f9b7e?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-02-28T04:43:54.188Z"},{"id":"hyjJ99jRI","title":"Keyword Generics Progress Report: February 2023","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/inside-rust/2023/02/23/keyword-generics-progress-report-feb-2023.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/keyword-generics-progress-report-february-2023-hyjj99jri","summary":"The post discusses the progress made by the Keyword Generics Initiative in introducing new syntax for async and const in Rust. It proposes the use of ?async and ?const notations for functions, traits, and types. It also explores the idea of introducing the effect/.do notation to mark functions as generic over modifier keywords. The post outlines the tentative plan for converting the designs into RFCs.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/10c030b2429f801a5aed8756bdece9d2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-02-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"gIadttvC8","title":"Why is building a UI in Rust so hard?","url":"https://www.warp.dev/blog/why-is-building-a-ui-in-rust-so-hard","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/why-is-building-a-ui-in-rust-so-hard--giadttvc8","summary":"Building a UI in Rust is challenging due to the language's unique memory management and lack of inheritance. Rust's ownership model and mutability rules make it difficult to share data across a component tree. However, there are different approaches like functional UI and Entity-Component-System architecture that can be used to overcome these challenges.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/fc370ced83ccc58c7a2013ebbdd03aff?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":49,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2023-02-17T00:35:03.267Z"},{"id":"0w_Y06mJG","title":"New release \u2013 gtk-rs","url":"https://gtk-rs.org/blog/2023/02/10/new-release.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-release-gtk-rs-0w-y06mjg","summary":"The new release of gtk-rs recommends upgrading to GTK4 and introduces improvements such as a new macro for using properties in glib::Object subclasses, direct conversions to glib::Value and glib::Variant, and support for subclassing gdk_pixbuf types. Other changes include new convenience traits, code generation improvements, better mapping of C ownership transfer, and new constructors for glib::Object. The release also includes updates to the GTK4 bindings and blueprint UI definition support.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/1a37c42a1d896bd25571c54154fba632","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-02-10T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"W6LtNOpkO","title":"Dramatically reducing AccessKit\u2019s memory usage","url":"https://accesskit.dev/dramatically-reducing-accesskits-memory-usage/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/dramatically-reducing-accesskit-s-memory-usage-w6ltnopko","summary":"A single large data structure for all accessible UI elements was a known weakness in AccessKit's design. The design flaw was a pressing problem that blocked users from using AccessKit. We decided to unblock further adoption of AccessKit and get the inevitable incompatible API changes out of the way sooner than later. This post summarizes the results of this optimization.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ddb88d9cba48778a07ad6c2851f02d5e","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-02-08T16:51:25.000Z"},{"id":"kZ005ZUoB","title":"Speeding up Rust semver-checking by over 2000x","url":"https://predr.ag/blog/speeding-up-rust-semver-checking-by-over-2000x/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/speeding-up-rust-semver-checking-by-over-2000x-kz005zuob","summary":"This post discusses how `cargo-semver-checks` can be significantly sped up by using the upcoming query optimization API in the Trustfall query engine. The post explains the challenges faced in checking large crates, the benefits of using indexes to improve query performance, and how Trustfall enables these optimizations without changing the lint rules.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d46095850a4d19abe7996b590832669a?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-02-07T23:17:53.222Z"},{"id":"y1S-sU3Tj","title":"Tauri vs Iced vs egui: Rust GUI framework performance comparison (including startup time, input lag, resize tests) \u00b7 Lukas\u02bc Blog","url":"http://lukaskalbertodt.github.io/2023/02/03/tauri-iced-egui-performance-comparison.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/tauri-vs-iced-vs-egui-rust-gui-framework-performance-comparison-including-startup-time-input-lag--y1s-su3tj","summary":"Comparison of the performance of Tauri, Iced, and egui as Rust GUI frameworks, including startup time, input lag, and resize tests.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5ee29174e3c1d36cb517430a3f0415ef?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-02-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"1zpIAIKQu","title":"Exploring Rust for Vulkan drivers, part 1","url":"https://www.collabora.com/news-and-blog/blog/2023/02/02/exploring-rust-for-vulkan-drivers-part-1/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/exploring-rust-for-vulkan-drivers-part-1-1zpiaikqu","summary":"This post explores the possibility of using Rust to write Vulkan drivers in Mesa. It discusses the benefits of Rust's safety features, the challenges of integrating Rust with C and C++ code, and the goals for creating clean and Rust-like wrappers for Vulkan objects.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/44d33f5ba8f02499403dbb0d22cdc1ed?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-02-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"eJID1akjC","title":"Rustler - Using Rust crates in Elixir","url":"https://mainmatter.com/blog/2023/02/01/using-rust-crates-in-elixir/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/rustler---using-rust-crates-in-elixir-ejid1akjc","summary":"Learn how to use Rust crates in Elixir with the help of Rustler. This post provides a step-by-step guide on setting up a project, implementing a PDF program, and exporting NIFs. Rustler allows for easy integration of Rust and Elixir, increasing performance significantly.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ecf58fe419772ee8a2668d8f6671a68f?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-02-01T00:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["kotlin","allthingssmitty","ardlbs","servlsst","andev"],"opposite_handles":["horde","dailydevworld","watercooler","on_leuwcq","alexfinn"],"similar":[{"id":"kotlin","handle":"kotlin","name":"Kotlin","is_squad":false,"x":-3.6552,"y":-2.7447,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":234,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/kotlin","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.633817,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.066239,"avg_read_time":2.974874,"tag_diversity":0.354701},"top_tags_preview":[["kotlin",1